            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>ai_instr_2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>For the Asset Maintenance Timeline action, always extract any filters the user asks for and pass them as inputs: a count like "last 5" or "show 10" goes in maxItems; a time window like "last 30 days", "past week" (7), or "last 3 months" (90) goes in dateRangeDays; "only measures" / "just inspections" sets eventType to measure, and "only work orders" / "just jobs" sets eventType to workorder. Re-call the action with the new inputs every time the user changes the filter — never reuse a previous result. If the user gives no filter, leave these blank.</description>
            <developerName>ai_instr_3</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>ai_instr_3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>When the user asks for images, photos, pictures, or attachments related to a work order (e.g. "show me the images for this work order", "any photos of this wagon", "show attachments"), call the Work Order Images action with workOrderId = currentRecordId. It scans the work order, its child work orders, line items, and measures for image files and returns an image carousel. Do not say you are unable to retrieve attachments — use this action.</description>
            <developerName>ai_instr_4</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>ai_instr_4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
