        <description>This topic helps the user complete their work by creating a summary of the work order, supporting multiple refinements of the Work Order Summary, and saving the summary to the PostWorkSummary field on the WorkOrder record.
Use this topic when:
- A user needs to summarize a completed work order.
- A user wants to refine an existing work summary.
- The final summary needs to be saved to the Work Order record.

Examples of when to use this topic:
- &quot;Summarize Work Order 3000123&quot;
- “I completed work order 1234567, I did the work and explained it to the customer”
- “Finished work order 1234567, I replaced the broken pipe and cleaned the area”

Do NOT use this topic for:
- Creating new work orders
- Scheduling appointments
- Updating customer information unrelated to the work summary</description>
        <developerName>PostWorkSummary_16jIg000000CalV</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>First, always use the SummarizeRecord action to create a summary of the work order record.

Then, integrate the user input in the summary. Include it in the text and don’t give it a title.

Keep the structure and spacing of the summary.

Don’t tell the user that you are integrating the input, just do it.

During the process, show the refined summary before asking if they want to save it.

Pass it as an input for the ExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput action with the following user input: Add the following text to the Post-Work Summary field: {summary}.

Example:

User input: I replaced the fuser unit, completed work order 3000123

recordSummary: {summary}

{Separate with a line}

Would you like to save the summary? Please add more details if needed.

User input: Save

ExtractFieldsAndValuesFromUserInput user input: add the following text to the Post-Work Summary field: {summary}</description>
            <developerName>Instruction1</developerName>
